IMPORT prelude

-- National Arts Council Act 1991 (Singapore) -- what the Council may give and charge (ss 2, 6(2)(d), (h)), where its money may and
-- may not go (ss 12(4), (5), 13 and First Schedule para 11), who may sue whom (s 24), who may sit on the Council and when a seat is
-- lost (s 4, First Schedule paras 2, 3, 8, 10), how its meetings decide (First Schedule para 12), its financial year and accounts
-- deadline (Second Schedule), the pension share for transferred civil servants (s 20(3)) and pension moneys out of creditors' reach
-- (Third Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NACA1991.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the SSO metadata
-- calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026. The latest amending Act annotated in the text and the Legislative History is
-- Act 2 of 2020 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2020, s 4).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0188 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance (statutory boards, institutions, government finance and pensions). It asks what the Act decides for a
-- person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Act is almost entirely constitutional: for an
-- artist or arts company, what it decides is that the Council MAY fund and charge them, on conditions it sets, and that its staff
-- are shielded from suit for good-faith acts. SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: the functions list (s 5) beyond its definition of
-- "the arts", patrons (s 7), ministerial directions (s 9), staff appointments (ss 10, 11, 11A), shares (s 12A), the 1991 transfer
-- of the National Theatre Trust and its employees (ss 15-19, 21-23) except the s 20(3) pension share, temporary appointments,
-- revocation and resignation (First Schedule paras 4-7, 9, 13), and the pension-trustee machinery (Third Schedule paras 5-8).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Arts Council Act 1991 -- the Council`

§§ `2, 6(2)(d) -- grants, loans and scholarships`

-- s 2: "'the arts' includes literary, performing and visual arts." The definition is inclusive, so a form not named (film, design,
-- craft) is neither in nor out on the words: the encoding can only say whether the Act NAMES it.
-- s 6(2)(d): the Council may "extend grants, contributions, loans or scholarships to any person or organisation connected with the
-- arts, subject to such conditions as the Council thinks fit". No eligibility test, amount, residence or citizenship condition and
-- no right to a grant appears anywhere in the Act.
DECLARE ArtForm IS ONE OF
    `literary arts`
    `performing arts`
    `visual arts`
    `film`
    `design`

GIVEN `the form` IS AN ArtForm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act names it as one of the arts` IF
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `literary arts` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `performing arts` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `visual arts` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `connected with the arts` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the Council's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may fund the applicant` IF
    `connected with the arts` AND `meets the Council's conditions`

-- Nothing in the Act turns the Council's power into a duty: "may" in s 6(2), and no entitlement provision anywhere. The rule
-- above therefore says only when funding is PERMITTED, never when it is owed. (Inference from the absence of any duty.)

-- s 6(2)(h): the Council may "charge fees, commissions or rent for any goods, services or facilities provided by the Council". No
-- scale, cap or approval of fees is set in the Act.
DECLARE CouncilProvision IS ONE OF
    `goods`
    `services`
    `facilities`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A CouncilProvision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may charge for it` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `goods` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `facilities` THEN TRUE

§§ `12(4), (5), 13 and First Schedule para 11 -- where the money may go`

-- s 12(4): funds and property "must be applied solely for the purposes of ... the functions, powers and duties of the Council ...
-- and no portion thereof may be paid or transferred, directly or indirectly, by way of dividend, bonus or otherwise by way of profit
-- to its members". (5): "Nothing in this section prevents the payment in good faith of remuneration to any employees".
-- First Schedule para 11: members are paid "such salaries, fees and allowances as the Minister may determine".
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a dividend to a member`
    `a profit-share bonus to a member`
    `fees and allowances to a member as the Minister determines`
    `good-faith salary to an employee`
    `a grant to an arts group under the Council's functions`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a dividend to a member` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a profit-share bonus to a member` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 13(1): the Singapore Arts Endowment Fund vests in the Council. (2): "Any interest, dividends and other income derived from the
-- Fund must be credited to the general funds of the Council." (4): "The Fund must not, except with the prior written approval of the
-- Minister, be applied, disposed of or alienated otherwise than as specified in section 12(2) and (3)" -- that is, kept in bank
-- accounts and invested under the standard investment power. So the Fund's CAPITAL cannot be spent on a grant without the Minister's
-- written approval; its INCOME, being credited to the general funds, can be (the second step is an inference from (2) and (3)).
DECLARE FundUse IS ONE OF
    `keeping it in a bank account`
    `investing it under the standard investment power`
    `paying a grant out of Fund capital`
    `paying a grant out of Fund income`

GIVEN `the use` IS A FundUse, `the Minister approved in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may be used that way` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `paying a grant out of Fund capital` THEN `the Minister approved in writing beforehand`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3, 24 -- who may be sued`

-- s 3: the Council is a body corporate "capable of (a) suing and being sued". s 24(1): "No suit or other legal proceedings shall lie
-- against any member or employee of the Council or other person acting under the directions of the Council for anything which is in
-- good faith done or intended to be done in the execution or purported execution of this Act." The shield is personal: it does not
-- protect the Council itself.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Council`
    `a member`
    `an employee`
    `a person acting under the Council's directions`
    `an unconnected person`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is within the shield` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `a member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person acting under the Council's directions` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 24 bars the suit` IF
        `the defendant is within the shield` `the defendant`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `in execution or purported execution of the Act`

§§ `4 and First Schedule paras 2, 3 -- size, terms and office-holders`

-- s 4(1): "The Council consists of not less than 11 but not more than 27 members."
GIVEN `members appointed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council's size is within section 4` IF
    `members appointed` AT LEAST 11 AND `members appointed` AT MOST 27

-- para 2(1): each member holds office "for a period of 3 years or for a shorter period the Minister determines"; (2) may be
-- re-appointed (no limit on re-appointments). para 3(1): the Chairperson is "a member (other than the Chief Executive)", the Deputy
-- "a member (other than the Chairperson or Chief Executive)", each for a period "not longer than 3 years". para 1(3): the Minister
-- may appoint the chief executive to be a member.
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is within the 3-year limit` IF
    `term in years` GREATER THAN 0 AND `term in years` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed Chairperson` IF
    `is a member` AND (NOT `is the Chief Executive`)

GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed Deputy Chairperson` IF
    `is a member` AND (NOT `is the Chief Executive`) AND (NOT `is the Chairperson`)

§§ `First Schedule paras 8, 10 -- disqualification and losing a seat`

-- para 10: a person "must not be appointed or continue to hold office as a member" if the person "(a) has a mental disorder and is
-- incapable of managing himself or herself or his or her affairs; (b) is an undischarged bankrupt or has made any arrangement or
-- composition with his or her creditors; or (c) is convicted of an offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude and has not
-- received a free pardon". On the words of (b), "has made" any arrangement disqualifies with no time limit, unlike "undischarged"
-- bankruptcy; and (c) has no spent-conviction period.
-- para 8: the office "must be vacated" if the member "(a) becomes in any manner disqualified ...; or (b) has been absent, without
-- leave of the Council, from 3 consecutive meetings".
DECLARE Person HAS
    `has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has made an arrangement or composition with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is disqualified from membership` IF
        `the person`'s `has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing own affairs`
    OR  `the person`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the person`'s `has made an arrangement or composition with creditors`
    OR  (`the person`'s `is convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `the person`'s `has received a free pardon`))

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member must vacate office` IF
        `the person is disqualified from membership` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3

§§ `First Schedule para 12 -- meetings`

-- para 12(1): the Chairperson may summon meetings "as often as may be required but not less than once in 3 months".
GIVEN `months since the last meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting interval complies` IF
    `months since the last meeting` AT MOST 3

-- para 12(2): "a quorum consists of half the total number of members appointed for the time being". With an odd number appointed,
-- half is not a whole number; the encoding reads it as at least half (present x 2 >= appointed), so 15 appointed needs 8. That
-- reading is an inference: the text does not say how to round.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `members appointed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `members appointed`

-- para 12(3): decisions "by a simple majority of the votes of the members present and voting; and in the case of an equality of
-- votes, the Chairperson or in the Chairperson's absence the Deputy Chairperson or the member presiding has a casting vote".
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the motion is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `casting vote is for`)

§§ `Second Schedule -- financial year and accounts`

-- para 1: "The financial year of the Council begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

-- para 2: the audited annual financial statements, signed by the Chairperson, go to the Minister "no later than 30 November in each
-- year", with any auditor's report. The encoding takes the sending date in the calendar year in which the financial year ended
-- (31 March), so the Council has eight months.
GIVEN `month sent` IS A NUMBER, `day sent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statements reached the Minister in time` IF
        `month sent` LESS THAN 11
    OR  (`month sent` EQUALS 11 AND `day sent` AT MOST 30)

§§ `20(3) -- the Government's share of a transferred officer's pension`

-- s 20(3): where a Government employee was transferred under s 18, "the Government is to be liable to pay the Council such portion of
-- any gratuity, pension or allowance ... as the same is to bear to the proportion which the aggregate amount of the person's
-- pensionable emoluments during the person's service with the Government bears to the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable
-- emoluments during his or her service under both the Government and the Council". The share is by EMOLUMENTS, not by years.
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A NUMBER, `Government emoluments` IS A NUMBER, `Council emoluments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share` MEANS
    `the benefit` TIMES `Government emoluments` DIVIDED BY (`Government emoluments` PLUS `Council emoluments`)

§§ `Third Schedule paras 1-4 -- pension moneys and creditors`

-- para 1: no payment under a s 20 pension scheme "is assignable or transferable, or liable to be garnished, attached, sequestered or
-- levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim other than a debt due to the Council or to the Government". para 3: such
-- moneys do not "pass to the Official Assignee on the bankruptcy of the contributor". para 4: salary deductions for the scheme
-- continue despite bankruptcy.
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the Council`
    `the Government`
    `a private creditor`
    `the Official Assignee in bankruptcy`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant can reach the pension moneys` IF
    CONSIDER `the claimant`
    WHEN `the Council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
